I. Adding the meta-mender-readonly-overlayfs layer to your build
=================================================

Run 'bitbake-layers add-layer meta-mender-readonly-overlayfs'

II. Purpose
===========

The layer contains an example setup for a Yocto build which enables
overlayfs support for docker and places the persistent data on the
Mender data partition

The example image "mender-readonly-overlayfs-image" does so based on a
`core-image-full-cmdline` image.

III. Included functionality
==========================

The `docker-overlayfs` is the main trigger to pull in `docker` and configure
it for `overlayfs`. The example image only installs this packages and
enables the `read-only-rootfs` `IMAGE_FEATURE`.